msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/automation/terraform/appDetail.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/automation/terraform/appDetail.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/terraform.rst:204
msgid ""
"When Terraform commands are executed against the application, |morpheus| "
"provides progress bars and command output in the UI. Command output is "
"shown underneath the Terraform command field. Users can dismiss "
"individual output windows by clicking the \"x\" button in the upper-right"
" of each window. All command output can be dismissed by clicking the blue"
" \"x\" button to the right of the command field itself."
msgstr ""
"When Terraform commands son executed against el application, |morpheus| "
"provides progress bars y command salida in el UI. Command salida es shown"
" underneath el Terraform command campo. Users puede dismiss individual "
"salida windows by clicking el \"x\" botón in el upper-right of cada "
"ventana. All command salida puede be dismissed by clicking el blue \"x\" "
"botón to el right of el command campo itself."

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/terraform.rst:206
msgid ""
"Within the ACTIONS reside four selections: Refresh State, Apply State, "
"Edit Inputs, and Edit STATE. Selecting Refresh State is equivalent to "
"using the \"terraform plan\" command from the command line. This will "
"read the existing state of any existing objects which are part of the App"
" and compare their current configuration against the prior state. Any "
"differences will be noted in the output. If differences are discovered, "
"the App is considered to be in a \"drift\" state. This drift status is "
"shown in the UI when the user is viewing the \"State\" subsection (which "
"is described in greater detail in the next section). The output of the "
"Refresh State command, including detailed information about changes "
"Terraform would make to App objects to in order to realign them with the "
"App spec are shown in the UI."
msgstr ""
"Within el ACTIONS reside four selections: Refresh State, Apply State, "
"Edit Inputs, y Edit STATE. Selecting Refresh State es equivalent to using"
" el \"terraform plan\" command desde el command line. This será read el "
"existente state of cualquier existente objetos cual son part of el App y "
"compare their actual configuración against el prior state. Any "
"differences será be noted in el salida. If differences son discovered, el"
" App es considered to be in un \"drift\" state. This drift estado es "
"shown in el UI cuando el usuario es viewing el \"State\" subsection (cual"
" es described in greater detalle in el siguiente sección). The salida of "
"el Refresh State command, including detailed información about cambios "
"Terraform sería make to App objetos to para realign them con el App spec "
"son shown in el UI."

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/terraform.rst:208
#, fuzzy
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/automation/terraform/planOutput.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/automation/terraform/planOutput.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/terraform.rst:210
msgid ""
"The Apply State selection brings up a modal which allows the user to view"
" the App spec once again. This includes being able to view and edit "
"Terraform variables if needed. After making any needed edits, click "
":guilabel:`NEXT` and |morpheus| will validate the App once again, just "
"like it did at provision time. On the next tab of the wizard, |morpheus| "
"will show the user and planned changes that would be executed if the user"
" completes the modal. An output will be shown as if \"terraform plan\" "
"were run from the command line. Make note of any App objects which would "
"be created, altered, or destroyed if the actions are accepted as "
"|morpheus| would immediately take them if desired. When ready, click "
":guilabel:`COMPLETE`. This will execute all planned changes as if the "
"user had run \"terraform apply -auto-approve\" from a terminal session."
msgstr ""
"The Apply State selection brings up un modal cual permite al usuario view"
" el App spec once again. This includes being able to view y edit "
"Terraform variables si es necesario. After making cualquier needed edits,"
" click :guilabel:`SIGUIENTE` y |morpheus| será validate el App once "
"again, solo like it did at provision time. En el siguiente pestaña of el "
"wizard, |morpheus| será show el usuario y planned cambios que sería be "
"executed if el usuario completes el modal. An salida se mostrará as if "
"\"terraform plan\" fueron run desde el command line. Make nota of "
"cualquier App objetos cual sería be creado, altered, o destroyed if el "
"acciones son accepted as |morpheus| sería immediately take them si se "
"desea. When ready, click :guilabel:`COMPLETE`. This será execute todos "
"planned cambios as if el usuario tenía run \"terraform apply -auto-"
"approve\" desde un terminal session."

